# Daniel Vu — Personal Website

Minimalist personal site built with Node.js + Express.

## Stack
- **Runtime**: Node.js 18+
- **Framework**: Express 4
- **Security**: Helmet (CSP, HSTS, etc.)
- **Contact form**: Server-side validation via express-validator, email via Nodemailer
- **Frontend**: Vanilla HTML/CSS/JS (no build step)

## Project structure
```
├── server.js            # Express app entry point
├── routes/
│   └── contact.js       # POST /api/contact endpoint
├── views/
│   ├── index.html       # Main page
│   └── 404.html         # 404 page
├── public/
│   ├── css/style.css    # Stylesheet
│   └── js/main.js       # Client-side form logic
├── .env.example         # Environment variable template
└── package.json
```

## Getting started

```bash
npm install
cp .env.example .env    # optional — fill in SMTP details to enable email
npm start               # production
npm run dev             # development with auto-reload (requires nodemon)
```

Site runs at **http://localhost:3000**

## Contact form

Without SMTP config, form submissions are logged to the console (useful for local dev).  
To enable real email delivery, set `SMTP_HOST`, `SMTP_USER`, `SMTP_PASS`, and `CONTACT_EMAIL` in `.env`.

## Deployment

Works out of the box on **Railway**, **Render**, **Fly.io**, or any Node.js host.  
Set `PORT` environment variable if needed (defaults to 3000).
